+    For each Gaussian $i$, the geometry parameters are predicted iteratively to refine the noisy initial positions:
+    a. Query the feature volume $F$ at the refined position $\mu^{init}_i + \Delta \mu^{prev}_i$ using trilinear interpolation to obtain feature vector $f_i$:
+    $$ f_i = F(\mu^{init}_i + \Delta \mu^{prev}_i) $$
+    b. Decode opacity and covariance using the MLP heads:
+    $$ \alpha_i = \mathcal{D}_{opa}(f_i), \quad \Sigma_i = \mathcal{D}_{cov}(f_i) $$
+    c. Decode the position offset $\Delta \mu_i$ using the position head, scaled by voxel size $v_{size}$:
+    $$ \Delta \mu_i = \text{Tanh}(\mathcal{D}_{pos}(f_i)) \cdot v_{size} $$
+    d. Update the Gaussian center:
+    $$ \mu_i = \mu^{init}_i + \Delta \mu_i $$
+    Here, $\Delta \mu^{prev}_i$ is the offset predicted in the previous iteration. This recursive formulation encourages the network to predict $\alpha_i$ and $\Sigma_i$ at accurate surface locations [S2].
